course: dictionary
lesson: 12709
title: Bossy words in stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what a person is like by showing what they do. When you meet a new word, look at the clues around it. «The domineering captain never let anyone else speak. He shouted orders and ignored every idea.» He does not let people talk and he ignores their ideas, so domineering must mean bossy and controlling.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «The bossy captain never let anyone else speak» and it still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Domineering is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a domineering parent or a domineering boss. Its verb is domineer, which means to control other people and push them around.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Domineering» means bossy and controlling in a strong, unpleasant way.
fact: «Domineer» is the verb: to control other people and tell them what to do without listening.
fact: A domineering person does not respect other people's choices.
fact: Phrases to remember: domineering parent, domineering boss, domineering manner.
exercise: «The domineering captain never let anyone else speak.» What does domineering mean? | Quiet and shy | *Bossy and controlling | Very tired | Kind and gentle
exercise: Which word is the verb from the same family as domineering? | sleep | sing | giggle | *domineer
exercise: «Ben's domineering sister chose every game and never asked what he wanted.» Which phrase shows she does not listen? | *never asked what he wanted | played outside | Ben's sister | chose every game
test: «The domineering boss changed everyone's plans without asking.» What does domineering describe? | A boss who loves music | *A boss who controls people and ignores their choices | A boss who gives everyone a day off | A boss who is always late
test: Which phrase describes someone who tells everyone what to do without listening? | cosy blanket | gentle whisper | *domineering manner | sunny morning
exam: Maya says domineering is just a fancy word for nice. Is she right? | *No, it means bossy and controlling | Yes, it means friendly | Yes, it means clever | No, it means noisy
